// # openOODA/Requirements.oot — The 10 Strategic Governance Requirements
//
// Logline: The 10 requirements that govern the openOODA polyrepo.
//          Authoritative reference; every repo must conform. Renamed
//          from "Pillars" to "Requirements" (2026-09-12 vocabulary
//          scrub; per RULES.oot §1.16).
//
// Setup:  This file replaces the "10 Pillars" framework previously
//         embedded in NORTHSTAR.oot §1.4. Each requirement maps to
//         one or more sections in RULES.oot. Requirements are
//         numbered for stable cross-reference; the names are the
//         content. Adding a requirement requires bumping RULES.oot
//         + updating the RULES cross-reference table below.
//
// Beats:
//   1. The 10 requirements.
//   2. RULES.oot cross-reference table.
//   3. Out-of-scope (what the requirements do not claim).

// ## 1. The 10 requirements

// ### Requirement 1 — First Principles & Pure File Extension Laws
//   Pure .oo and .oot files only. Derive algorithms and grammar
//   directly from hardware specs, IEEE 754, NIST KATs, and IETF
//   RFCs. See RULES.oot §1.1.

// ### Requirement 2 — Performance & Subtractive Design
//   Strict <= 256 lines per file. Maximize instruction throughput.
//   Minimize runtime overhead via linear arenas and O(1) resets.
//   Zero intermediate artifacts in std/. See RULES.oot §1.2, §1.8.

// ### Requirement 3 — Adversarial Validation & Double-Run Invariant
//   8-Dimensional Red Team verification (e1..e8) and 8-Gate Blocking
//   Veto Protocol. Double-run tests: Run_1(Test) == Run_2(Test).
//   See RULES.oot §1.10.

// ### Requirement 4 — Academy 4-Element Headers
//   ASD-STE100 headers (# Title, Logline, Setup, Beats on .oo;
//   Title, File on .oot (2-line clean header; version SSoT is git
//   tags plus per-repo VERSION files per RULES.oot §1.21)).
//   See RULES.oot §1.11.

// ### Requirement 5 — Capability Security & Zero Ambient Authority
//   20 language tokens (FsReadCap, FsWriteCap, ..., CompilerReadCap)
//   + 26 substrate caps — 20 subset of 26, SSoT is
//   oodar sec/cap/caps.h / cap_table.json. Compile-time SMT check
//   elision and self-hosted bootstrapping. See RULES.oot §1.18.

// ### Requirement 6 — Multi-Process Coordination Safety
//   Stationary workspace topology (Delta_path = 0). Fail-closed
//   fork bomb rejection, AST reflection (`ooda outline`),
//   automated repair (`ooda fix`), and collaborative multi-process
//   protocols. See RULES.oot §1.6.

// ### Requirement 7 — Formal RFC Template Compliance
//   All RFCs in rfcs/ follow 0000-template.oot with mandatory
//   Security and Testing sections. See RULES.oot §1.13.

// ### Requirement 8 — Two-Binary Architecture
//   Decoupled compiler (oodac) and product CLI driver (ooda).
//   See RULES.oot §1.14.

// ### Requirement 9 — C/H Substrate Isolation
//   Low-level C shims (oodar.c, oodar.h, types.h) strictly confined
//   to the oodar/ repo. Zero C header leaks into openOODA/std/.
//   The oodar/ repo is the canonical home of the C host substrate;
//   its public ABI is the set of oo_* symbols exported by the 6
//   per-domain subdirs (core, sec, fs, net, hw, app) per the
//   v2.0.0 6-subdir layout. See RULES.oot §1.14.

// ### Requirement 10 — Clean Workspaces
//   Zero loose unheaded .oo files in roots, zero struct trailing
//   commas, clean workspace. See RULES.oot §1.14.

// Plus the three operational laws (RULES.oot §1.20):

// ### Subtractive Optimization
//   Improve software by removing unneeded runtime state and
//   ambient privileges.

// ### Deterministic Execution
//   Produce bit-identical binaries with zero-timestamp digests.

// ### 100% Specified Contracts
//   Every public function documents its contract: inputs,
//   preconditions, postconditions, failure modes.

